Frozen structural signature for PASSWORD_ASSIGN, checked by tools/run_tests.sh SUPERSET. Regenerated 2026-09-05 (second time same day): the first regeneration for ROW-150/151/152 froze the backstop arm's operator AFTER it had regressed from `\s*` to `[ 	]*(?:?
[ 	]*)*`, which silently dropped 25 whitespace codepoints (NBSP among them) the old bare-keyword arm always covered -- this baseline's own SUPERSET check could not see that regression because it compares the arm's text to ITSELF, so it locked the narrowing in rather than flagging it. A critic caught it by fuzzing, not by reading this file. This regeneration restores `\s*` on both sides of the operator; see record/findings/row-150-151-152-cross-product-gaps-and-the-backstop-arm.md. Regenerated again 2026-09-09 for ROW-238: the backstop and weak arms' tail extension widened from `[ 	]` to `[^\S
]` (any whitespace but newline), closing the same separator leak CREDENTIAL_ASSIGN had (NBSP, EN SPACE, VERTICAL TAB, FORM FEED, LINE SEPARATOR U+2028, a bare CR all crossed `[ 	]` without ending a `
`-delimited line). No lookaround was added or removed; this is the same class of change ROW-152's own regeneration note describes as safe to make without extending the lookaround census, a widening of what gets swallowed once the rule has already fired, not of when it fires. Regenerated again 2026-09-17 for PH-488: `[^\S
]` itself was the wrong separator class -- it crosses CR and U+2028/U+2029, which a real document can use as its own line ending, so a CR-only or U+2028-only passport had everything after its first credential line DELETED, not redacted (record/findings/backend-row-201-238-reconcile-fixes-four-leaks-and-regresses-cr-and-line-separator-documents.md). Both arms' tail now use a named separator class (literal space/tab plus the Unicode Zs space-separator characters) that excludes every character a real document can use as a line ending, an accepted narrowing of the leak class itself (a passphrase using bare CR/U+2028/U+2029 as an internal word separator is no longer redacted past it), not of when the rule fires. No lookaround was added or removed.
